company.description:
eToro Acquires MPC Wallet Firm Zengo For $70 Million To Push Into Self-Custody

@eToro CEO Yoni Assia (@yoniassia) took the stage at Paris Blockchain Week on Wednesday to announce the trading platform has officially acquired self-custodial crypto wallet provider Zengo. Bloomberg reports the deal is worth around $70 million, paid mostly in cash. It pairs eToro's 40 million registered users with Zengo's keyless wallet technology, which uses multi-party computation (MPC) cryptography.

Assia framed the move as a bet on user-controlled finance, calling self-custody core to the future of digital finance and saying the deal bridges TradFi and the crypto-native world in one app. The acquisition positions eToro to support DeFi use cases including prediction markets and perpetuals.

@ZenGo had previously raised $24 million total, with backing from Insight Partners and Tether, and acquired stablecoin wallet Minke last year. eToro shares were up more than 6% on the news and 18% over the past week.

